From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 01:24:36 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 085/147] hjviewer: fixes from the 1.8.2 screen review
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The PC home: P1's title is short enough for the 200 px pane ("서버에 연결되지
않음", two lines at most), its buttons grow with an English label of two lines
and sit 8 px apart, P2's and P3's home lines are a title of one line with
until when below it, and the home follows a ticket taken or ended at once
(a hint of the state the registering process notes next, at most 30 s). G3
is as high with its [로그인] as without; the left pane shows its scrollbar
while it scrolls; the ID menu opens beside the card and its tooltip above.

Confirms: the logout of all other devices has its title, the gate's line is
a second paragraph 8 px down and no longer repeats the question, a phone's
logout on a staff-only server is a danger confirm, and a recent card's
removal says what goes with it and ends in [지우기]. A form error in P3 says
the code's form instead of E6; the offline text names the support code while
the server trades them; S2 keeps one width and draws its error and its end
as P3's. Korean breaks at spaces in the confirms, the field errors, the
pane's texts, the 내 PC placeholder and the About notes.

Smaller: the device name without a doubled platform, [로그아웃] without the
name, "Log in"/"Log out" in English, the About update lines in English and
in line on a phone, the phone ID label in the theme's tertiary text, the
phone settings' off switches on a visible track, a lighter off knob on the
desktop, the 내 PC note beside a short host name, [지원 코드 만들기] in the
desktop tab bar, the ID suggestions say that Enter connects, the right-
clicked card keeps its border while its menu is open, ko.rs "… 사용".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
